You can save a JavaScript object to `localStorage` by first converting it to a JSON string using `JSON.stringify()`. To read it back, use `JSON.parse()` on the string retrieved from `localStorage`. Here's an example:

```javascript
// Save object to localStorage
const myObject = { name: "John", age: 30 };
localStorage.setItem("user", JSON.stringify(myObject));

// Read object from localStorage
const storedObject = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem("user"));
console.log(storedObject.name); // Outputs: John
```

This method ensures the object is properly serialized and deserialized.
